right now volunteers from across our  state are in Florida ready to assist  along with more than 500 Red Cross  disaster relief workers from around the  nation they want to make sure that  everyone impacted by the storm has a  safe place to stay food to eat relief  supplies and emotional support executive  director Rachel Flanagan says our  volunteers move supplies into place late  last week to be able to accommodate 60  000 people initially  a lot of our folks have deployed to the  Orlando area just to be away from the  storm and then they're going to work  their way towards those zones it looks  like they're on standby but we will more  than likely be deploying our emergency  response vehicle which is our big  feeding truck that we have that will  more than likely be leaving southern  Nevada here towards the end of the week  to deploy to that region as well all the  trucks in the country are actually on  standby  Flanagan reminds everyone to also donate  blood depending on the severity of the  storm more blood may be needed in the  Florida area now if you would like to  help people impacted by this storm visit  redcross.org call 1-800 Red Cross or  simply text the word Red Cross to 90999  to make a 10 donation we do have all  this information as well as a link to  the American Red cross's site to help  out as a whole on our website
 

